# ============================================================
# ITM Server Security Monitor
# Trusted network policy
#
# Installed to /etc/security-monitor/trusted_networks.conf
#
# Used by the audit modules to decide whether a remote address
# is inside the managed estate. An outbound session from a root
# process to an address outside these networks is a finding.
#
# One entry per line. IPv4 CIDR, or a bare address. Comments
# start with #. RFC1918 space and loopback are always treated
# as private, whether or not they are listed here.
#
# The installer generates this file from the TRUSTED_NETWORKS
# value in install.sh, which is the same list used for the
# Fail2Ban ignoreip policy, so both stay in step.
# ============================================================

127.0.0.0/8
::1

# ITM management networks
192.168.100.0/24
192.168.111.0/24
103.166.224.0/24
